{le cevni kurji ko} isn't an expression, but two sumti stuck side by side;
if you use {cevni kurji ko}, you are commanding someone (or something) to
[let it/him/her-self} be taken care of by god, which is closer to the
meaning, but still not quite there.

On the topic of curses: even though it's important to be able to understand
novel phrases and to be able to come up with them when necessary, it's also
important to have a cache of canned constructions for expressing oneself
without needing to think too hard about it.

